# Master Data — Dropdown Options

All **dropdown / select options** in the School CRM dashboard must come from **`GET /api/v1/master-data`** (Bearer auth). Do not hardcode option arrays in page mocks or utils.

## Endpoint

| Property | Value |
|----------|--------|
| URL | `GET /api/v1/master-data` |
| Response | `{ success, message, data: { role: [...], gender: [...], ... } }` |
| Item shape | `{ id, label, value }` |

## Infrastructure

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/apis/masterDataApi.js` | `getMasterData()` |
| `src/context/masterDataContext.jsx` | `MasterDataProvider` on dashboard layout — one fetch, shared app-wide |
| `src/hooks/useMasterDataSelect.js` | `useMasterDataSelect(key, { placeholder, prepend, useIdAsValue, ... })` |
| `src/utils/masterDataOptions.js` | `MASTER_DATA_KEYS`, `getMasterDataOptions`, `getMasterDataIdOptions`, `buildSelectOptions` |

Use **`useIdAsValue: true`** when the form stores numeric FK ids (class, academicYear, user). Use **value** field for enums (gender, role, status codes).

## `data` keys (API)

`role`, `userStatus`, `gender`, `bloodGroup`, `religion`, `community`, `medium`, `studentStatus`, `feesPaymentStatus`, `primaryContact`, `documentVerificationStatus`, `schemeType`, `discountType`, `applicableTo`, `termType`, `feeBillingTerm`, `paymentMode`, `ledgerStatus`, `invoiceStatus`, `paymentRecordStatus`, `feeCategory`, `academicYear`, `section`, `class`, `classReference`, `feeHead`, `user`

## Screen mapping (integrated)

| Screen | Master-data keys |
|--------|------------------|
| User Creation | `role`, `userStatus` |
| Admission setup | `class`, `academicYear` (id) |
| Admission student | `gender`, `bloodGroup`, `religion`, `community` |
| Admission parents | `primaryContact` |
| Students filters | `class`, `section`, `academicYear` (+ “All” prepend from mock label only) |
| Fee Head config | `class`, `academicYear`, `feeBillingTerm` |
| Create fee head modal | `feeCategory` (+ Yes/No for mandatory/refundable/active — boolean UI, not master data) |
| Payments collect | `user`, `feeBillingTerm`, `paymentMode` (tiles) |
| Reports filters | `academicYear`, `class`, `termType` (period/month) |
| Transfer Certificate | `user` (student); reason = text input (no API key yet) |
| Staff add modal | `role`; department = text input |

## Dropdown UI — one style app-wide (mandatory)

**Every dropdown** in the dashboard uses **`FormSelect`** / **`FormScrollSelect`** — the same custom control as admission **Academic year** (not native `<select>`).

Implementation: `src/components/reusable/js/formScrollSelect.jsx` (`formSelect.jsx` re-exports it).

| Requirement | Implementation |
|-------------|----------------|
| Trigger | Rounded field + chevron; blue focus ring when open |
| Menu | White panel, rounded, shadow; opens in a **portal** (`document.body`) so lists are not clipped |
| Active item | Light blue background + primary blue text (`.crmScrollSelectOptionActive`) |
| Scrollable list | `overflow-y: auto` on `.crmScrollSelectMenu` |
| Hidden scrollbar | `.crmScrollSelectMenu` in `src/styles/scrollSmooth.css` |
| Smooth scroll | `scroll-behavior: smooth` via `scrollSmooth.css` |
| Compact height | `max-height: 8rem` (~4–5 items); option padding `0.375rem 0.5rem` |
| `onChange` | Synthetic event: `onChange={(e) => setX(e.target.value)}` |

Do **not** add native `<select>`, MUI Select, or custom one-off dropdowns. Use `variant="filter"` for toolbar filters (no label).

## Rules

1. Mocks: labels, placeholders, validation copy only — **no `options: [...]`** for master-data fields.
2. Loading: disable dropdown while `useMasterDataSelect` / context `isLoading`.
3. Add new keys to `MASTER_DATA_KEYS` when API docs add fields.
4. New scrollable dropdown panels: ensure selector is in `scrollSmooth.css`.
